# Optional per-system tweaks for removable-media automounting
# (/usr/lib/hwsupport/steamos-automount.sh).
#
# This file is sourced by the automount helper when present. Uncomment a line
# to override the built-in default. The defaults shown are the built-ins.
#
# Mount options per filesystem. Extra options are automatically allowed for
# the udisks2 mount, so plain, filesystem-agnostic additions (e.g. nodiratime)
# work as-is.
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_EXT4_MOUNT_OPTS="rw,noatime"
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_F2FS_MOUNT_OPTS="rw,noatime"
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_BTRFS_MOUNT_OPTS="rw,noatime"
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_VFAT_MOUNT_OPTS="rw,noatime,uid=1000,gid=1000,utf8=1,umask=000,flush"
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_EXFAT_MOUNT_OPTS="rw,noatime,uid=1000,gid=1000"
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_NTFS_MOUNT_OPTS="rw,noatime,uid=1000,gid=1000,windows_names"
#
# btrfs main subvolume to mount (default "@"). Empty to disable subvolume
# mounting and show the top-level.
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_BTRFS_SUBVOL="@"
#
# Opt-in: bind mount the internal compatdata over steamapps/compatdata on
# Windows-formatted (vfat/exfat/ntfs) drives so Proton games start from them.
# Tradeoff: the Steam client can no longer eject the drive.
# ARMADA_AUTOMOUNT_COMPATDATA_BIND_MOUNT="0"